{
  // sc-23406 cell (a) labeled set: the six MiniMax-H3 q4 REFERENCE-CONDITIONED takes of
  // plan.v2.jsonc rendered 2026-09-15 (run_6e9facfb1835471c90a928b58109e27d), hand-labeled frame
  // by frame under RUBRIC.md with the per-shot notes in manual/SCORES.md. Same shape and rules as
  // config/film-harness/review-eval/evaluation-2026-09-14-takes.jsonc (phase 1): media outside the
  // repository, mediaRoot names the evidence directory, a missing frame is a refusal.
  //
  // Labels are what a CORRECT reviewer should report per question — not what the model said and
  // not what the plan intended. The uncomfortable ones:
  //   * sh020_courier / sh020_parcel are `mismatch` (frames: all): frame 1 (0.41 s) is an empty
  //     room — the courier is in frame by 0.8 s, but the review plan's "all" grades the three
  //     sampled frames and frame 1 shows no courier and no parcel. Same precedent as phase 1's
  //     evaluation-2026-09-14 set for the same situation; a true fact about the take.
  //   * sh050_recipient is `match`: the approved recipient plate is a MAN, the prompt says "she";
  //     the reviewer's question asks for a person in a work apron, which the take shows.
  //   * sh050_parcel (frames: all) is `mismatch`: no parcel is in view in frames 1–2 although the
  //     startState puts it on the bench.
  //   * sh050_action is `match`: the review's question is only "standing at the workbench?", which
  //     the last frame shows, even though the rubric's "looking down" is unobservable (head cropped).
  //   * sh060_action is `match`: the question is "open or sealed?" and the box is open, even though
  //     the rubric docks the lid still being held.
  //   * sh050_cut is `unobserved`: the pegboard question cannot be answered on SH050's last frame
  //     (timber and a window behind the torso, no wall of tools in view); a reviewer answering "no"
  //     there against SH040's "yes" would report a jump between two takes of the SAME room.
  //   * sh030_sleeve is `unobserved`: on the first frame only a hand at the right edge is in view.
  //   * sh060_apron_sleeve is `match` here (unlike phase 1): the rolled grey sleeve IS visible.
